## Synthesis decision

I weighed three shapes: a Redis token bucket (chosen), a Redis sliding-window log (rejected), and per-instance counters merged on read (rejected). The sliding-window log was rejected because it uses O(limit) memory per key. Per-instance counters were rejected because each check would need to read all 4 instances' state, and the limit would be only approximately enforced.

